Z||000000||curtis||01-06-2001||07:06 PM||||I just bought the second passenger side caliper from Oreilly auto parts. It remanufactured. When I install the brake line  bolt it strips it out. This is the second one. The other side did fine.Please help.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Bob Englert||01-06-2001||07:33 PM||||I had the same problem with my daughter's 87 coupe.  Went through 3 calipers before I got one that would hold.  I have gotten very gunshy about torquing doen the brake hose bolts.  Now I am very careful and try to tighten them down just enought to prevent fluid leakage.  <P>I think the Haynes manual said to torque them to 30 ft-lbs.  This is WAY too much.  Probably 10-12 ft-lbs is better.<P>I would get the auto parts store to replace the caliper and try again.  Be gentle!  If all else fails you might try a new caliper instead of the reman.  The threads will be in better shape with the new caliper.<P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
Z||000002||mrfiero||01-06-2001||07:57 PM||||What you are experiencing is bad helicoiling.  I have had this occur several times with remanufactured calipers.  <P>Bottom line is it is not your fault....keep returning them until you get a good one.<P><BR>||||reg||1
